font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T18:43:26-07:00","id":1196305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1194594-how-precisely-to-invictus-oath-s-work?p=1196301#post1196301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is specifically a benefit <i>from</i> the Oath of Penance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct and I spoke too soon. Sorry for that.<br /> <br /> I echo Tessie's point that it likely breaks the oath to attack your Liege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T14:53:05-07:00","id":1196615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1194594-how-precisely-to-invictus-oath-s-work?p=1196305#post1196305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are correct and I spoke too soon. Sorry for that.<br /> <br /> I echo Tessie's point that it likely breaks the oath to attack your Liege.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True on that. but many kindred might be able to carry out an assasination in one stroke...<br /> <br /> <br /> or do you have a better idea of how to enjoy the immunity to your lieges disciplines? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T15:38:24-07:00","id":1196628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1194594-how-precisely-to-invictus-oath-s-work?p=1196615#post1196615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True on that. but many kindred might be able to carry out an assasination in one stroke...<br /> or do you have a better idea of how to enjoy the immunity to your lieges disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, intent to break the Oath may be sufficient, depending how one models the Oath's power and what was actually swore.<br /> <br /> As for enjoying immunity to your Lieges disciplines, maybe you aren't suppose to enjoy it. Maybe exposing yourself via this Oath enacts a kind of mercy from your Liege's Beast. It wouldn't break the Oath to feel secure that your Liege won't fuck with you. Maybe that is it's purpose; to allow vampire submission.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd likely use it to establish friendship with a Venture. Knowing they can alter your mind and memory, I'd be wrecked by paranoia. Others too, making it hard to connect to the Venture, something they'd feel. A means to exist on the same level might allow for a closer bond. Again, it is about submission. &quot;I am your lesser, you need not fear me. As you don't fear me, I need not fear you striking me.&quot; End result: Relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T06:34:26-07:00","id":1197576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1194594-how-precisely-to-invictus-oath-s-work?p=1196628#post1196628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for enjoying immunity to your Lieges disciplines, maybe you aren't suppose to enjoy it. Maybe exposing yourself via this Oath enacts a kind of mercy from your Liege's Beast. It wouldn't break the Oath to feel secure that your Liege won't fuck with you. Maybe that is it's purpose; to allow vampire submission.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd likely use it to establish friendship with a Venture. Knowing they can alter your mind and memory, I'd be wrecked by paranoia. Others too, making it hard to connect to the Venture, something they'd feel. A means to exist on the same level might allow for a closer bond. Again, it is about submission. &quot;I am your lesser, you need not fear me. As you don't fear me, I need not fear you striking me.&quot; End result: Relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, to me, the point of Oaths and Law in particular: they give teeth to the efforts of vampiric society to manage their monsters in a way that enables everyone to feel secure around other dreadful predators. Invictus ossify everyone into defined roles and strata, ensuring that at any time you can check yourself and know if X or Y is a threat, and thereby mollify your beast so you can get on with being genteel. The hierarchy literally gives them power. Carthians similarly benefit from extending the reach of their Laws to as many as possible--the wisdom of crowds and the assent of the governed literally gives them power.<br /> <br /> The other Covenants have looser ways of handing status and position signaling, such as Ordo titles and the like. But the point is the same: enabling vamps to get on without having to constantly expend precious blood stamping down or controlling those who should be subordinates, or subordinates playing dominance games to avoid being utterly crushed. If you can reliably get your result with a few social skill rolls, then that's better than needing to hit a couple extra blood bags and deal (later) with someone who's pissed they were Dominated!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}